    <bpmn:process id="W_W4014" name="W4014. Sourcing Decision, Pause &amp; Exit (Responsible Disengagement) Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Uncorrected critical finding; unremediated abuse; sourcing decision
Frequency: On event
Volume: High-risk suppliers as needed
Owner: VP Supply Chain / Sustainability/ESG Manager
Participants: Procurement (links to VS-03/VS-122/VS-67), Sustainability, Merchandising (links to VS-01), Legal (links to VS-100), Supply Planning (links to VS-02), Compliance
Source: workflow W4014 — Sourcing Decision, Pause &amp; Exit (Responsible Disengagement) Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4014_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4014_Lane1" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4014_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4014_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4014_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4014_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4014_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4014_Start3" name="Uncorrected critical finding; unremediated abuse; sourcing decision">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4014_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4014_Task4" name="Procurement/Sustainability integrate human-rights performance into sourcing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Procurement/Sustainability integrate human-rights performance into sourcing decisions: prefer compliant/improving suppliers; pause new orders for unremediated critical findings; and weigh responsible disengagement as a last resort per UNGP (leverage, not reflexive exit)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Sustainability / Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4014_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4014_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4014_Task5" name="Procurement/Sustainability manage responsible exit where required: phased…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Procurement/Sustainability manage responsible exit where required: phased disengagement, mitigate harm to workers (avoid sudden mass job loss), source alternatives (links to VS-122/VS-03), and protect supply continuity (links to VS-02)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Supply Planning / Sustainability
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4014_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4014_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4014_Task6" name="Procurement/Sustainability document the decision basis (links to VS-88), report…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Procurement/Sustainability document the decision basis (links to VS-88), report to governance/Board (links to VS-36/W4017), and apply lessons to risk model (W4006) and sourcing strategy (links to VS-122)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Sustainability / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4014_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4014_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4014_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4014_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-624 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Human Rights Risk Assessment, Auditing &amp; Remediation (PA-131.2).) | - operational: UNGP leverage-first principle; operational: phased approach and alternatives
Owner: VP Supply Chain / Sustainability/ESG Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4014_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4014_Annotation8" targetRef="W4014_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
